// The proofs and the feel's metrics (design.md, "The agent loop"). A proof is a recorded run:
// pads and how long each is held, from a course's start state. Each must keep reaching its goal
// in exactly the ticks it took when it was recorded, so a change to the movement that breaks a
// route, or moves its time, fails here; re-record a proof only when the change is meant. The
// metrics measure the movement in metres and ticks, against the ranges each preset is held to.
// The contract tests check the rules of design.md's contracts one at a time.

use body::{Body, Mode, RADIUS, spawn}
use course::LAB
use feel::{FEELS, MOMENTUM, STEP, feel}
use pad::{DOWN, Hold, JUMP, PRESS, Pad, RIGHT, RUN, UP, hold}
use std::hash::state_hash
use std::io::print
use world::{play, step, world}

// ---- proofs ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The lab from its start to its goal with the momentum preset: over the crest, both gaps and both
/// steps at a run, down the slide and off its lip, into the pool, a dive, and a dolphin leap up
/// the far wall. Recorded from the first lab's autopilot.
